Now that you mention undead, shouldn't chaotics have some way of
creating undead pets?  Say, if you are chaotic and sacrifice a non-fresh
corpse at an altar, it becomes a pet zombie?  That may be too easy,
though, so how about either a spellbook of animate dead or making the
animate feature only work at altars with priests or making it a gift
from your god:
#offer <gray dragon>
You feel that Loki is pleased  -more-
You notice the gray dragon corpse twitching -more-
You stop to avoid hitting you're gray dragon zombie

To limit this you may want to restrict the feature to only work on 
humanoids, or say that manufactured undead decompose and dissolve after
a certain number of turns, or do really irritating things like, say, 
attack the oracle or a shopkeeper (or you).  Also, a wand of turn undead
might serve to manufacture zombies, or, for chaotics, to tame existing
ones.

Suggestion and/or flames welcome.

